  "prefLabel": "Geo 307.01 License",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Geo 307.01 License. An applicant for licensure as a professional geologist, who has met satisfactorily all the requirements of RSA 310-A and who has paid all of the fees, shall be issued a license by the board. The licensee shall be issued a license authorizing the practice of geology that shall show the name of the licensee, have a serial number, and be sealed and signed by the members of the board.\n\nSource. #7526, eff 7-1-01; ss by #9439, eff 3-25-09; ss by #12152, eff 3-24-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/geo100-500.html"
